 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Foundation Models Comparison: TimesFM vs Chronos 2\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook provides a comprehensive comparison of two state-of-the-art foundation models for time series forecasting:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **TimesFM 2.5** (Google Research): Decoder-only transformer pre-trained on 100B+ time points\n",
    "- **Chronos 2** (Amazon Science): T5-based model with language model techniques\n",
    "\n",
    "Both models support **zero-shot forecasting** - making predictions without any training!\n",
    "\n",
    "**What you'll learn:**\n",
    "- How each model performs on the same data\n",
    "- Key differences in capabilities and design\n",
    "- When to use each model\n",
    "- Performance characteristics (speed, accuracy)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Installation Requirements\n",
    "\n",
    "Both models have specific installation requirements:\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "# For TimesFM\n",
    "git clone https://github.com/google-research/timesfm.git\n",
    "cd timesfm\n",
    "pip install -e \".[torch]\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# For Chronos 2\n",
    "pip install 'darts[chronos]'\n",
    "# or\n",
    "pip install chronos-forecasting>=2.0.0\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Imports"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type":": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import time\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from darts import TimeSeries\n",
    "from darts.datasets import AirPassengersDataset, EnergyDataset\n",
    "from darts.models import TimesFMModel, ChronosModel, ExponentialSmoothing\n",
    "from darts.metrics import mape, rmse"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Load Test Data\n",
    "\n",
    "We'll use the classic Air Passengers dataset for our comparison."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load Air Passengers dataset\n",
    "series = AirPassengersDataset().load()\n",
    "train, val = series.split_before(0.8)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Training data: {len(train)} points\")\n",
    "print(f\"Validation data: {len(val)} points\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Visualize\n",
    "series.plot()\n",
    "plt.title(\"Air Passengers Dataset (1949-1960)\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Passengers (thousands)\")\n",
    "plt.axvline(x=train.end_time(), color='r', linestyle='--', label='Train/Val Split')\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Side-by-Side Zero-Shot Forecasting\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's test both models on the same forecasting task **without any training**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### TimesFM Zero-Shot Forecast"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Initialize TimesFM\n",
    "timesfm_model = TimesFMModel(zero_shot=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Time the prediction\n",
    "start_time = time.time()\n",
    "timesfm_forecast = timesfm_model.predict(n=len(val), series=train)\n",
    "timesfm_time = time.time() - start_time\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate error\n",
    "timesfm_mape = mape(val, timesfm_forecast)\n",
    "timesfm_rmse = rmse(val, timesfm_forecast)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"TimesFM Results:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  MAPE: {timesfm_mape:.2f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"  RMSE: {timesfm_rmse:.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Inference Time: {timesfm_time:.2f}s\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Chronos 2 Zero-Shot Forecast"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-10",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Initialize Chronos 2\n",
    "chronos_model = ChronosModel()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Time the prediction\n",
    "start_time = time.time()\n",
    "chronos_forecast = chronos_model.predict(n=len(val), series=train)\n",
    "chronos_time = time.time() - start_time\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate error\n",
    "chronos_mape = mape(val, chronos_forecast)\n",
    "chronos_rmse = rmse(val, chronos_forecast)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Chronos 2 Results:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  MAPE: {chronos_mape:.2f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"  RMSE: {chronos_rmse:.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Inference Time: {chronos_time:.2f}s\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-11",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Visual Comparison"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-12",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Plot side-by-side comparison\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(15, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "# TimesFM plot\n",
    "ax = axes[0]\n",
    "series.plot(ax=ax, label=\"Actual\", linewidth=2)\n",
    "timesfm_forecast.plot(ax=ax, label=\"TimesFM Forecast\", linewidth=2, linestyle='--')\n",
    "ax.axvline(x=train.end_time(), color='r', linestyle=':', alpha=0.5)\n",
    "ax.set_title(f\"TimesFM 2.5\\nMAPE: {timesfm_mape:.2f}% | Time: {timesfm_time:.2f}s\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Passengers (thousands)\")\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Chronos 2 plot\n",
    "ax = axes[1]\n",
    "series.plot(ax=ax, label=\"Actual\", linewidth=2)\n",
    "chronos_forecast.plot(ax=ax, label=\"Chronos 2 Forecast\", linewidth=2, linestyle='--')\n",
    "ax.axvline(x=train.end_time(), color='r', linestyle=':', alpha=0.5)\n",
    "ax.set_title(f\"Chronos 2\\nMAPE: {chronos_mape:.2f}% | Time: {chronos_time:.2f}s\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Passengers (thousands)\")\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle(\"Zero-Shot Forecasting Comparison\", fontsize=14, fontweight='bold', y=1.02)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-13",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Overlay Comparison"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-14",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Single plot with both forecasts\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
    "series.plot(label=\"Actual\", linewidth=2.5, color='black')\n",
    "timesfm_forecast.plot(label=f\"TimesFM (MAPE: {timesfm_mape:.2f}%)\", linewidth=2, linestyle='--', marker='o')\n",
    "chronos_forecast.plot(label=f\"Chronos 2 (MAPE: {chronos_mape:.2f}%)\", linewidth=2, linestyle='--', marker='s')\n",
    "plt.axvline(x=train.end_time(), color='r', linestyle=':', alpha=0.5, label='Train/Val Split')\n",
    "plt.title(\"Direct Comparison: TimesFM vs Chronos 2\", fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Passengers (thousands)\")\n",
    "plt.legend(loc='upper left')\n",
    "plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-15",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
